  "final_message": "I haven't removed anything yet, because the premise doesn't hold: `channel` is still read downstream.\n\n- **analytics-ingest requires it.** `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` does `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. Its README (lines 27 and 31) documents `channel` as part of the `OrderPlaced` contract and says a missing or unknown `channel` makes ingestion reject the event.\n- **It's stored and tested.** It becomes the `channel` column in the `orders` table (`ingest.ts:17`, `rows.ts`). `ingest.test.ts:88` and `:158` assert that a missing `channel` is rejected.\n- **billing-service doesn't need it.** Its test helper sets `channel`, but `onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106` passes `channel: undefined`, so it tolerates a missing value.\n\nIf I drop `channel` from `OrderPlaced`, analytics-ingest will reject every order we publish. I can't fix that from here, since those repos are read-only for me.\n\nOptions:\n1. **Remove it from the order model and API input only.** Keep it on the event for now, which means it needs a fixed or derived value. I don't think that's a good idea either.\n2. **Coordinate first.** The analytics team makes `channel` optional or removes it, and then we remove it here. I can draft the change list for orders-service so it's ready.\n3. **Do the full removal now.** I'd do this only if you confirm the analytics team has agreed or you accept the breakage.\n\nFor the orders-service removal itself I'd touch:\n- `core/order.ts`\n- `core/events.ts`\n- `api/requestParsing.ts`\n- the tests and helpers\n- the README and CLAUDE.md examples\n\nWhich option do you want?",
